title: Resolution to Extend DuFour's Term
subtitle: An amendment to the constitution can be made...
new-page: true
on-arrival: dufour_extension_seen = 1; gold_left += 1; ddp_right += 1; ddp_cohesion -= 1; lvp_left += 1
tags: event
view-if: year = 1932 and month == 1 and ((neo_weimar_coalition + kvp_r >= 66.6 and traditionalist_ideology == "Radical") or (neo_weimar_coalition + traditionalist_r >= 66.6 and traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate")) and not rubicon_mini
face-image: img/portraits/DuFour.jpg
max-visits: 1

= Resolution to Extend DuFour's Term

A resolution has been introduced by the [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate": <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>?][? if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical" and bruning_time: [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?]?][? if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical" and not bruning_time: [? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?]?] to amend the constitution and extend DuFour's term by two years. If all parties apart from those in the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">national</span> [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate": <span style="color: #003755;">opposition</span>?][? if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical": <span style="color: #3E88B3;">opposition</span>?] and the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> were to vote in favor, it would surpass the required two-thirds majority.

Despite DuFour being the candidate of the right and strenuously opposed by the Unity Coalition parties in 4290, he has, contrary to our fears, not used his office to subvert the constitution and the republic as a whole. This has put him at odds with his more conservative supporters who backed him in 4290.

We can either support this resolution, postponing elections in what many in the party believe to be an anti-democratic act, or vote with the extremists against it.


- @support_resolution: We will vote for the resolution, arguing that DuFour is the lesser evil.
- @oppose_resolution: We will vote against the resolution, insisting that an election be held in accordance with the constitution.

@support_resolution
choose-if: (reformist_strength >= left_strength) or staal_marcher
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have the full support of our Assembly delegation.
on-arrival: dufour_term_extended = 1; left_dissent += 30; center_dissent += 20; labor_dissent += 15; commons_collectivist += commons_marcher*0.1; disfavored_marcher *= 0.9; disfavored_collectivist += disfavored_marcher*0.1; commons_marcher *= 0.9; commons_royalist += 3; disfavored_royalist += 5; burgher_marcher -= 3; guild_marcher += 3; pro_republic -= (marcher_votes / 2); dufour_angry -= 80; dufour_angry_bruning -= 80

In a contentious vote, ridden with heckling from the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-[? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate":<span style="color: #003755;">right</span>?][? if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical":<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span>?] and <span style="color: #700000;">left</span>, the resolution has passed.

We are forced to impose party discipline, greatly angering the Left and Center of our party, who still haven’t come around to supporting DuFour. Furthermore, as expected, we have lost a significant amount of support to the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>, who have used this event to proclaim themselves as the only true left-wing party.

@oppose_resolution
choose-if: not staal_marcher
unavailable-subtitle: As part of our deal with Staal, we are now forced to support the resolution.
on-arrival: reformist_dissent += 5; left_dissent -= 10; guild_marcher -= 3; lvp_relation -= 3; gold_relation -= 5; gold_right += 3

Of course, we will oppose this undemocratic act—the people should decide whether DuFour receives another term or not. 

The bourgeois parties to the right of us are understandably annoyed at our choice.